<title>SINGAPORE: Kuwait sells term naphtha - table of buyers.</title>
<headline>Kuwait sells term naphtha - table of buyers.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1997-02-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>State-owned Kuwait Petroleum Corp (KPC) has sold 2.7 million tonnes of full-range naphtha on term between March 1997-February 1998 to buyers in Japan, South Korea and India, industry sources said on Friday.</p>
<p>They said KPC renewed the contracts with 10 buyers from Japan for 1.5 million tonnes and four from South Korea for 900,000 tonnes.</p>
<p>It signed a new contract with India's Reliance Industries for 300,000 tonnes, the sources said.  </p>
<p>Reliance was seeking supplies to for its 700,000 tonnes-per-year petrochemical plant, which started up in December and was due to operate at full capacity in March.</p>
<p>KPC set a record price of $13.50 per tonne over Mideast spot quotes on a free-on-board basis for the supplies.</p>
<p>The term volume agreed in the latest talks by buyers was as follows (in thousand tonnes):</p>
<p>    JAPAN     Mitsubishi Chemical	300</p>
<p>		  Shell Japan		  300</p>
<p>		  Petrodiamond		 200</p>
<p>		  Idemitsu		     150</p>
<p>		  Marubeni		     100</p>
<p>		  Mitsui Corp		  100</p>
<p>		  Nissho Iwai		  100</p>
<p>		  Sumitomo		     100</p>
<p>		  Fuji Oil		     100</p>
<p>		  Nippon Oil		    50</p>
<p>    S. KOREA  Daelim			 300</p>
<p>		  LG Caltex		    200</p>
<p>		  Ssangyong		    200</p>
<p>		  Hanwha			 200</p>
<p>    INDIA     Reliance		     300</p>
<p>    TOTAL VOLUME			    2,700</p>
<p>--Singapore Newsroom (+65-870-3086)</p>
</text>
